      "body": "# PR type\n- [x] Bug Fix\n- [ ] New Feature\n- [ ] Document Updates\n- [ ] More Models or Datasets Support\n\n# PR information\n\nFixes #10473\n\n## Summary\n\n`check_json_format` handled only Python scalars and standard containers, then fell back to `obj.__dict__` for anything else. NumPy scalars (`np.float32`, `np.int64`, `np.bool_`) and arrays have no `__dict__`, so writing eval metrics such as the InfoNCE `mean_neg` / `mean_pos` values to `logging.jsonl` raised:\n\n```text\nAttributeError: 'numpy.float32' object has no attribute '__dict__'\n```\n\nThis converts NumPy scalars with `.item()` and `np.ndarray` with `.tolist()`, then recurses through `check_json_format`, so nested arrays end up as plain Python values that `json.dumps` accepts. Non-NumPy values keep their previous behavior.\n\n## Verification\n\nBefore (current `main`):\n\n```text\nfloat32 ERR AttributeError 'numpy.float32' object has no attribute '__dict__'\nint64   ERR AttributeError 'numpy.int64' object has no attribute '__dict__'\nbool_   ERR AttributeError 'numpy.bool_' object has no attribute '__dict__'\nndarray ERR AttributeError 'numpy.ndarray' object has no attribute '__dict__'\n```\n\nAfter:\n\n```text\n$ .venv/bin/python -m pytest tests/utils/test_check_json_format.py tests/utils/test_format_time.py -q\n6 passed, 1 warning in 2.25s\n```\n\nThe new `tests/utils/test_check_json_format.py` covers NumPy scalars, numeric and nested arrays, a metrics dict mimicking the training log payload, and unchanged behavior for plain Python values.\n\nLint:\n\n```text\nflake8 swift/utils/utils.py tests/utils/test_check_json_format.py\nisort --check-only ...\nyapf --diff ...\n# all clean\n```\n\nNo GPU or model download is required for this change.\n\n# Checklist\n\n- [x] I have linked the related issue above, if there is one.\n- [x] I have reviewed and understand every changed line, and I can explain how the change works and why it is correct.\n- [x] I have run the relevant tests or reproductions locally, and included the commands and results above (if applicable).\n- [x] I am responsible for the content of this PR, regardless of how it was produced.\n",
